# A pointer cast given directly to a Structure formal keeps its operand's sources (l2_reference_source), and they
# reach the formal as a call's result does (RECEPTION-EDGE-DEBTS (c)): the formal's reads take them by name.  run's
# p is an opaque formal.  The root gives it an Other whose `value` is its second field: 9.  Until 2026-10-05 the
# formal was read by position and gave the Other's first field, 1, with no refusal.  A Model: 4.  Entry 7.
Model:
    size_t: value 4U
end: Model

Other:
    size_t: pad 1U
    size_t: value 9U
end: Other

base: merge: Model
wide: merge: Other

fn: get (Model: x) size_t
return: x\value

fn: run (@: void p) size_t
return: get((cast: (@: void) p))

size_t: a run(wide)
size_t: b run(base)
int: ok 7
if: a = 1U
    ok: 61
if: a != 9U && a != 1U
    ok: 81
if: b != 4U
    ok: 82
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
